From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:33:53 +0200
Subject: clk: intel: grx500: register the gates the packet datapath draws on

The gate table carries twelve peripheral gates and none of the three the
packet datapath runs on, even though the bit position of each is already
defined beside the others: the buffer manager at bit 9 of the first gate
status register, the packet accelerator at 26 and the switch at 28.

That has cost nothing so far, because a gate nobody registers is a gate
the framework cannot turn off either.

Register all three the way the rest of the table is registered, with
CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED like every gate above them. Nothing holds these three
yet, so that flag is the whole of what keeps clk_disable_unused away from
clocks the packet datapath does not survive losing, which is the policy
the comment over the table already states. The same comment already names
the buffer manager, the packet accelerator and the switch among them; this
is what makes that sentence true of the table under it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c b/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
index b3447f43cb13..6e2c2559d94c 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/intel/clk-grx500.c
@@ -124,6 +124,12 @@ static struct intel_clk_branch grx500_branch_clks[] __initdata = {
 	 * PAE, GSWIP and both USB controllers; the packet datapath does not
 	 * survive losing them.
 	 */
+	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_CBM, "g_cbm", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
+		   G_CBM_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
+	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_PAE, "g_pae", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
+		   G_PAE_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
+	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_GSWIP, "g_gswip", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED,
+		   GRX500_CLK_GSR1, G_SWITCH_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
 	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_DMA0, "g_dma0", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
 		   G_DMA0_SHIFT, GATE_CLK_HW, 0),
 	INTEL_GATE(GCLK_USB0, "g_usb0", NULL, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, GRX500_CLK_GSR1,
